1
00:00:02,221 --> 00:00:07,366
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, Madinan Period, Volume 2

2
00:00:07,723 --> 00:00:09,911
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,446 --> 00:00:14,714
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:14,754 --> 00:00:16,429
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُه’

5
00:00:16,947 --> 00:00:22,716
We're finishing with some miscellaneous events concerning Fath e Makkah(فتح مكه),

6
00:00:23,437 --> 00:00:24,453
In Sha Allah O Ta'ala (اِنْ شاءالله تعالى).

7
00:00:24,651 --> 00:00:31,737
Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he entered into Makkah he chose a Mo'azzin(مؤذن), someone to call the Adhan(آذان).

8
00:00:32,543 --> 00:00:37,883
And the particular choice of Rasool Allah ﷺ was Bilal Ibn Rabah رضي الله عنه.

9
00:00:38,810 --> 00:00:43,911
And Rasool Allah ﷺ had Bilal(بلال) climb over Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) to deliver the Adhan(آذان).

10
00:00:44,371 --> 00:00:47,858
According to Younas Bin Mukhair(يونس بن مخير), Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered

11
00:00:47,988 --> 00:00:51,008
 اَمَرَبِلَالً اَنْ يُؤَذَنَ لِيَغِيْظَ بِهِ الْمُشْرِكِيْنْ

12
00:00:51,816 --> 00:00:56,643
Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal(بلال) to give Adhan(آذان) in order to anger the polytheists.

13
00:00:57,116 --> 00:00:58,826
Because Bilal(بلال) was seen as a slave,

14
00:00:59,385 --> 00:01:03,076
and now he's calling to the Salah(صلاة), and he's climbing over Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) to do it.

15
00:01:03,775 --> 00:01:09,076
And therefore there were some narrations of comments made by the people of Makkah

16
00:01:09,494 --> 00:01:14,851
showing their displeasure with the fact that Bilal(بلال) was the one, who is calling the Adhan(آذان),

17
00:01:15,018 --> 00:01:21,226
like one of them said; Can you see this black crow barking from on top of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

18
00:01:21,266 --> 00:01:25,766
 and things like that derogatory terms made by the Mushrikeen(مشركين) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

19
00:01:25,814 --> 00:01:31,029
Rasool Allah ﷺ, intended to have Bilal(بلال) make the Adhan(آذان) to show them

20
00:01:31,635 --> 00:01:35,634
just what we were talking about before, the new era that Islam is bringing,

21
00:01:35,937 --> 00:01:40,466
where class and caste of Jahilliyah(جاهلية) do not matter anymore

22
00:01:40,774 --> 00:01:46,185
and it is Taqwa(تقوى) that makes a person high or low.

23
00:01:46,296 --> 00:01:54,025
It is according to how close they are to Allahعَزّوجَلّ, it is their Taqwa(تقوى) it is their following of Islam.

24
00:01:54,390 --> 00:01:59,199
 And according to Saeed Bin Musayyib رحمه الله,

25
00:01:59,742 --> 00:02:03,433
that particular day when the people entered into Makkah

26
00:02:03,929 --> 00:02:06,692
it wasn't a day of celebration, it wasn't a day of partying.

27
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:07,301
It says;

28
00:02:07,405 --> 00:02:11,023
فَلَمَّا كَانَ لَيْلَةْ دَخَلَ النَّاسِ مَكَّه، لَيْلَةَ الْفَتْحْ

29
00:02:11,539 --> 00:02:15,870
لَمْ يَزالُ فِيْ تَكْبِيْرٍ، وَ فِيْ تَهْلِيْلٍ ، وَ فِيْ طَوَافٍ بِالْبَيْتْ حَتَّى اَصْبَح

30
00:02:16,461 --> 00:02:21,058
فَقَالَ اَبُوْ سٌفِيَّانْ لِهِنْدْ اَتَرَيْنَ هَذَا مِنَّ الله ، قَالَ : نَعْمْ ، هَذا مِنَّ الله

31
00:02:21,773 --> 00:02:24,972
When the people entered into Makkah, the day of conquest,

32
00:02:25,304 --> 00:02:28,543
they remained in Takbeer(تكبير) and Tahleel(تحليل).

33
00:02:28,812 --> 00:02:29,724
 Tahleel(تحليل) meaning saying;

34
00:02:29,764 --> 00:02:30,780
 لَا اِلَهَ اِلَّا الله

35
00:02:31,054 --> 00:02:33,261
And Takbeer(تكبير) means saying Allah-Ho-Akbar(الله اكبر)

36
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:37,269
and Tawaf Bil Bait(طواف بِالْبَيت) circling Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

37
00:02:37,785 --> 00:02:40,727
They've been away from Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) for a long time.

38
00:02:41,214 --> 00:02:48,507
And now they are pleased and happy that Allahعَزّوجَلّ allowed them to enter into Makkah and to worship Allah

39
00:02:48,713 --> 00:02:53,002
according to the rules of Islam, while Islam is dominant in Makkah.

40
00:02:53,395 --> 00:03:00,367
So, they were making Tawaf(طواف) around the house all the way until, the morning there was Ibadah(عبادة), all night

41
00:03:00,581 --> 00:03:02,335
all night long, there was Ibadah(عبادة).

42
00:03:02,708 --> 00:03:06,977
Wherever you go in Makkah you can see people making Takbeer(تكبير) and making Tahleel(تحليل)

43
00:03:07,222 --> 00:03:09,665
and making Tawaf(طواف) around the house of Allah.

44
00:03:09,916 --> 00:03:12,223
So, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) went back to his wife and said;

45
00:03:12,589 --> 00:03:13,977
Do you think this is from Allah?

46
00:03:14,199 --> 00:03:22,872
I mean, it's an impressive scene, it's something that even affected these people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) people of Makkah,

47
00:03:23,111 --> 00:03:25,133
who are just moments ago Kuffar(كفار).

48
00:03:25,916 --> 00:03:28,125
So Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) told his wife:

49
00:03:28,165 --> 00:03:29,819
اَتَرَيْنَ هَذَا مِنَّ الله

50
00:03:30,004 --> 00:03:31,313
Do you think this is from Allah?

51
00:03:31,506 --> 00:03:33,475
She said: Yes, this is from Allah.

52
00:03:34,066 --> 00:03:35,991
And then Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) met Rasool Allah ﷺ.

53
00:03:36,031 --> 00:03:37,554
 And Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

54
00:03:37,987 --> 00:03:42,101
You told Hind(هند): Do you think this is from Allah?

55
00:03:42,534 --> 00:03:45,098
And Hind told you: Yes, I think this is from Allah.

56
00:03:45,590 --> 00:03:46,573
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said;

57
00:03:46,925 --> 00:03:49,315
I testify that you are the Messenger of Allah.

58
00:03:49,545 --> 00:03:54,688
 No one overheard our conversation, there was no one there but we, me and Hind(هند).

59
00:03:55,363 --> 00:03:58,555
Rasool Allah ﷺ said as narrated by Al-Bukhari(اَلْبُخَارِيْ);

60
00:03:58,823 --> 00:04:02,576
إنَّ الله حَرَّمَ مَكَّةَ يَومَ خَلَقَ السَّمَوَاتِ والأرْضَ

61
00:04:03,113 --> 00:04:08,117
فَهِيَّ حَرَامٌ بِحَرَمَ اللَّهِ إلى يَومُ الْقِيَامَةِ، لَا تَحِلُّ لِأحَدٍ قَبْلِي

62
00:04:08,489 --> 00:04:13,727
وَلَا تَحِلُّ لِاَحَدٍ بَعْدِيْ ، وَلَمْ تَحْلُلْ لِيْ إلَّا سَاعَةً مِنَّ الدَّهَر

63
00:04:14,114 --> 00:04:21,836
لَا يُنَفَّرُ صَيْدُهَا، وَلَا يُعْضَدُ شَوْكُهَا، ولَا يُخْتَلَى خَلَاهَا، ولَا تَحِلُّ لُقَطَتُهَا، إلَّا لِمُنْشِطْ

64
00:04:22,362 --> 00:04:27,141
Allah has made Makkah as a sanctuary, the day He created the heavens and the earth

65
00:04:27,708 --> 00:04:30,894
it is the sanctuary by Allah's having made it so,

66
00:04:31,569 --> 00:04:34,743
and will remain such until, the Judgment Day.

67
00:04:35,172 --> 00:04:41,602
Conflict in it was not made permissible for anyone before myself, nor for anyone after me.

68
00:04:41,973 --> 00:04:44,188
And this only for a short time.

69
00:04:44,657 --> 00:04:52,306
In it, gain may not be hunted, it's trees may not be cut down, nor mates vegetation be uprooted

70
00:04:52,768 --> 00:04:58,059
and items found in it, belong to the Finder only after announcement of the Find.

71
00:04:58,893 --> 00:05:05,381
Al-Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib رضي الله عنه want to exclude from this rule a plant called Al-Izkhar(ألإذخر).

72
00:05:05,573 --> 00:05:08,096
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ said: You're not allowed to cut down trees.

73
00:05:08,372 --> 00:05:10,529
So, Al-Abbas(العباس) wanted to exclude the Al-Izkhar(ألإذخر) .

74
00:05:10,932 --> 00:05:15,826
Because they use it for the dead, it's a fragrant tree, it has a nice smell to it.

75
00:05:16,323 --> 00:05:20,265
And apparently it's also used as fuel for blacksmiths

76
00:05:20,383 --> 00:05:22,811
 because in another narration says; Lil-Qaim(لِلْقَيْمْ).

77
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:25,842
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said except for Al-Izkhar(ألإذخر).

78
00:05:26,088 --> 00:05:31,084
Rasool Allah ﷺ allowed them to cut down this particular plant or a tree but nothing else.

79
00:05:31,369 --> 00:05:37,208
 So, Makkah and also Madina are Haram(حرام) and they are a sanctuary,

80
00:05:37,597 --> 00:05:42,399
and hunting is not allowed there in and uprooting trees is not allowed.

81
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:48,056
There's a Hadith(حديث) by Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه, we go through it In Sha Allah(اِنْ شَاالله).

82
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:49,762
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) says, that

83
00:05:50,018 --> 00:05:55,736
delegations went to meet Muawiya(معاويه), so we're talking about a long time after the Fath(فتح) of Makkah(مكه).

84
00:05:56,495 --> 00:05:59,197
We're talking about in the time, when Muawiya(معاويه) was a Khalifah(خليفه)

85
00:05:59,699 --> 00:06:02,185
وَذَالِكَ فِي رَمَضَانْ and that was during the time of Ramadan(رمضان).

86
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:04,919
فَكَانَ يَصْنَعُ بْعْضُنَا لِبَعْضِ الطَّعَامْ

87
00:06:05,401 --> 00:06:09,158
So, we would prepare food for each other.

88
00:06:09,498 --> 00:06:16,654
And this shows you the social aspect of the, life of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and Tabieen(تابعين)

89
00:06:16,963 --> 00:06:19,244
these were delegations that were there.

90
00:06:19,634 --> 00:06:25,045
And rather than everybody having their meal alone, they would invite each other.

91
00:06:26,041 --> 00:06:30,576
So, Abu Hurairah(ابو هريره) said; I invite you to my place.

92
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,781
Now, Abu Hurairah(ابو هريره) it says in this narration.

93
00:06:33,821 --> 00:06:36,451
 مِمَّا يُكْثِرْ اَنْ يَدْعُوْنَا الى رَحْلِهْ

94
00:06:36,776 --> 00:06:40,201
He was the most who would invite us, he would invite us the most.

95
00:06:41,010 --> 00:06:47,244
So, one of At-Tabieen(تابعين), wanted to invite Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه,

96
00:06:47,589 --> 00:06:48,488
so he said;

97
00:06:48,648 --> 00:06:51,834
 فَقُلْتُ اَلَا اَصْنَعَ طَعَامً فَاَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلَى رَحْلِيْ

98
00:06:51,882 --> 00:06:55,919
So I decided that I'm going to invite them to my place this time.

99
00:06:56,641 --> 00:06:59,851
Obviously, these are not permanent dwellings, they are all visitors.

100
00:07:00,399 --> 00:07:03,232
فَاَمِرْتُ بِطَعَامٍ يَصْنَعْ، ثُمَّ لَقِيْتُ اَبَا هُرَيْرَةْ

101
00:07:03,272 --> 00:07:05,785
I prepared the food and then I met Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره)

102
00:07:06,388 --> 00:07:07,133
and I told him;

103
00:07:07,196 --> 00:07:08,181
اَلدَّعْوَةْ عِنْدِيْ اَلْلَيْلَةْ

104
00:07:08,221 --> 00:07:11,609
Invitation is at my place tonight.

105
00:07:11,815 --> 00:07:12,061
 He said;

106
00:07:12,101 --> 00:07:12,719
 اَسْبَقْتَنِيْ

107
00:07:12,950 --> 00:07:14,145
He said: you beat me to it.

108
00:07:14,546 --> 00:07:15,372
I said: Yes.

109
00:07:16,648 --> 00:07:20,546
So, Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره), when he arrived at the gathering,

110
00:07:21,221 --> 00:07:24,527
he wanted to make it a beneficial gathering. So, he said;

111
00:07:24,562 --> 00:07:27,271
اَلَا اعْلِمَكُمْ بِحَدِيْثٍ مِنْ حَدِيْثِكُمْ، يَا مَعْشَرِالْاَنْصَارْ؟

112
00:07:27,522 --> 00:07:32,177
Shouldn't I tell you a Hadith(حديث) that belongs to you, O people of Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار)

113
00:07:32,257 --> 00:07:34,810
apparently most of these people who were there, were from Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار).

114
00:07:35,216 --> 00:07:36,779
ثُمَّ ذَكَرَ فَتَحْ مَكَّةْ فَقَالْ

115
00:07:36,959 --> 00:07:40,293
So, he talked about the story of the conquest of Makkah.

116
00:07:40,671 --> 00:07:46,784
He said, when Rasool Allah ﷺ came to Makkah he sent Az-Zubair(ألزبير) on one of the two wings of the army,

117
00:07:47,084 --> 00:07:50,238
and he sent Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) commanding the other wing

118
00:07:50,539 --> 00:07:54,039
 and Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) was commanding the foot soldiers.

119
00:07:54,253 --> 00:07:59,734
 So, they entered into Makkah and Rasool Allah ﷺ, was in his battalion.

120
00:08:00,008 --> 00:08:03,155
So, he saw me and he said: O Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) I told him;

121
00:08:03,195 --> 00:08:04,497
لَبَّيْكَ يَا رَسُوْل الله

122
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:08,807
So, he said: No one but the Ansaar(أنْصَار) should come to me.

123
00:08:09,538 --> 00:08:14,620
So, this was a private gathering that Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to have with Al-Ansaar(ألْأنْصَار).

124
00:08:15,236 --> 00:08:18,146
So, Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) went and invited the Ansaar(أنْصَار), he called them,

125
00:08:18,193 --> 00:08:21,758
 so they came and surrounded Rasool Allah ﷺ from every direction.

126
00:08:22,003 --> 00:08:24,891
 قُرَيْشْ وَبَشَتَ لَهَا اَوْبَاشًا

127
00:08:25,398 --> 00:08:28,573
Quraish(قريش) has mobilize the force of some men.

128
00:08:28,977 --> 00:08:34,519
And these were people from the outskirts of Makkah to fight,

129
00:08:34,852 --> 00:08:37,820
 but they didn't risk themselves going into the fight.

130
00:08:38,203 --> 00:08:42,966
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they mobilize this force but they themselves did not join and they said;

131
00:08:43,006 --> 00:08:46,139
 If they win then we will join if they lose then we're safe.

132
00:08:46,769 --> 00:08:48,198
And you can't win in this way.

133
00:08:48,238 --> 00:08:49,937
If you don't want to participate yourself,

134
00:08:50,015 --> 00:08:55,787
if you don't want to be in the front line like Rasool Allah ﷺ, like the Sahabah(صحابه) were there's no hope of winning.

135
00:08:56,073 --> 00:09:03,542
So, those who are hiding and sending their foot soldiers to do all the work,

136
00:09:04,114 --> 00:09:09,008
while they are cowering behind and hiding, they will not win.

137
00:09:09,327 --> 00:09:15,193
So these Aobaash(أوباش) these people who are supposed to fight for Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they were defeated.

138
00:09:15,549 --> 00:09:16,669
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

139
00:09:16,762 --> 00:09:23,613
اَتَرَوْنَ اِلَى اَوْبَاشٍ قُرَيْش وَاَتْبَاعِهِمْ؟ ثُمَّ قَالَ بِيَدَيْهِ اِحَدَاهُمَا عَلَى اُخْرَى، ثُمَّ قَالَ حَتَّى تُوَافُوْنِيْ بِالصَّفَا

140
00:09:23,912 --> 00:09:27,780
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave his orders to fight these Aobaash(أوباش)

141
00:09:27,843 --> 00:09:31,048
and many of them were killed and then the fighting stopped.

142
00:09:31,571 --> 00:09:34,182
Anyway, they ended up meeting on As-Safah(اَلصَّفاء).

143
00:09:35,191 --> 00:09:39,586
And when they met with Rasool Allah ﷺ, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

144
00:09:40,229 --> 00:09:43,239
 مَنْ دَخَلَ دَارْ اَبِيْ سُفِيَان فَهُوَ آمِنْ

145
00:09:43,667 --> 00:09:47,991
whoever, enters into the house of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), he is safe.

146
00:09:48,484 --> 00:09:54,603
Rasool Allah ﷺ has announced that whoever enters into the house of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) is safe.

147
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:58,487
Now the house of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) is not gonna be enough for all of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), obviously

148
00:09:58,841 --> 00:10:04,614
but Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to give Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) this honor to draw him closer to Islam.

149
00:10:04,858 --> 00:10:05,876
 But he also said:

150
00:10:06,154 --> 00:10:08,376
وَمَنْ دَخَلَ مَنْزِلَه’ فَهُوَ آمِنْ

151
00:10:08,416 --> 00:10:12,709
 Whoever enters into his house, he will be safe, so no one will attack you in your house.

152
00:10:12,773 --> 00:10:15,765
But if we see you on the streets then you will be killed.

153
00:10:16,249 --> 00:10:20,874
So, it's like a curfew, nobody is allowed to leave their homes.

154
00:10:21,477 --> 00:10:28,098
 And Rasool Allah ﷺ after this conflict happened,

155
00:10:28,374 --> 00:10:38,767
the Ansaar رضي الله عنهم, they felt that Rasool Allah ﷺ now because he's back in his hometown, he might leave them and stay behind.

156
00:10:39,216 --> 00:10:43,203
 Now, he's with his clan, he's with his relatives he's in Makkah.

157
00:10:43,521 --> 00:10:45,374
 So, he's going to leave us that's the end.

158
00:10:45,634 --> 00:10:47,809
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ called them and said;

159
00:10:48,530 --> 00:10:53,281
أقُلْتُمْ اَمَّا رَجُلْ فَاَدْكْتُه’ رَغْبَةَ فِيْ قَرْيَتِه ، قَالُوْ قَدْكَانَ ذَالِكْ

160
00:10:53,343 --> 00:10:56,392
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them: Did you say so? They said: Yes.

161
00:10:56,836 --> 00:10:58,773
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

162
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:01,200
 اِنِّيْ عَبْدُالله وَرَسُوْلُه

163
00:11:01,415 --> 00:11:03,495
I am the servant of Allah and His messenger.

164
00:11:03,994 --> 00:11:05,751
هَاجَرْتُ اِلَى الله وَاِلَيْكُمْ

165
00:11:06,121 --> 00:11:08,477
I made Hijrah(هجرة) to Allah and to you.

166
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:12,049
فَالْمَحْيَا مَحْيَاكُمْ وَالْمَمَاتُ مَمَاتُكُمْ

167
00:11:12,292 --> 00:11:14,646
Life is with you, and death is with you.

168
00:11:14,872 --> 00:11:16,297
فَاَقْبَلُوا الَيْه يَبْكُوْنَ

169
00:11:16,609 --> 00:11:19,106
So, they came crying to Rasool Allah ﷺ, and they said;

170
00:11:19,527 --> 00:11:22,442
وَلله مَا قُلْنَا اَلَّذِيْ قُلْنَا اِلَّا الظنْ بِالله وَرَسُوْلِه

171
00:11:22,482 --> 00:11:28,286
We only said, what we said because of our eagerness and desire to have you with us

172
00:11:28,326 --> 00:11:32,180
and our love of Allah and love of His messenger.

173
00:11:32,871 --> 00:11:34,099
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

174
00:11:34,361 --> 00:11:36,556
اِنَّ الله وَرَسُوْلَه يَصَدِّقَانِكُمْ

175
00:11:36,796 --> 00:11:39,034
Allah and His Messenger believe you.

176
00:11:39,555 --> 00:11:44,748
Safwaan Ibn Umayyah(صفوان إبن أمية) was one of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) he fled

177
00:11:45,181 --> 00:11:50,803
because he thought, he has done so much against Islam and Rasool Allah ﷺ would kill him.

178
00:11:51,117 --> 00:11:54,349
Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب), his close friend in Jahilliyah(جاهلية)

179
00:11:54,384 --> 00:11:56,466
and if you remember, we talked about Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب).

180
00:11:56,973 --> 00:12:01,690
Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) is the man whom Safwaan(صفوان) sent to assassinate Rasool Allah ﷺ

181
00:12:02,116 --> 00:12:07,809
and when he arrived in Madina, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him about his plan to come and assassinate him.

182
00:12:08,271 --> 00:12:13,482
So, he was shocked that Rasool Allah ﷺ knew the details of this plan and he ended up becoming Muslim.

183
00:12:14,641 --> 00:12:19,563
So, now Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) when he heard about Safwaan(صفوان) running away he followed him.

184
00:12:19,769 --> 00:12:23,912
Safwaan(صفوان) went to Jeddah to ride a boat and go to Yemen.

185
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:28,734
So, Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) told him; I have come to you from Rasool Allah ﷺ

186
00:12:28,910 --> 00:12:30,988
because Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) spoke to Rasool Ullah and said;

187
00:12:31,484 --> 00:12:35,302
O Messenger of Allah Safwaan(صفوان) is the leader of his people give him immunity.

188
00:12:35,533 --> 00:12:38,072
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I will give him immunity.

189
00:12:38,404 --> 00:12:40,697
Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) said give me a sign, a token.

190
00:12:41,157 --> 00:12:43,266
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him his turban,

191
00:12:43,657 --> 00:12:48,292
as a sign of the fact that Rasool Allah ﷺ is giving Safwaan(صفوان) immunity.

192
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:52,093
Umair(عمير) took the turban of Rasool Ullah and he went to meet Safwaan(صفوان).

193
00:12:52,127 --> 00:12:53,730
 Safwaan(صفوان) told him; Stay away from me.

194
00:12:53,952 --> 00:12:59,664
Umair(عمير) said; I have come to you from the Most Merciful and from the most compassionate man, and the most forgiving

195
00:13:00,181 --> 00:13:05,307
and his kingdom is yours and this position is yours and his honor is yours.

196
00:13:05,505 --> 00:13:07,616
He's telling him that he's your relative

197
00:13:08,130 --> 00:13:12,279
and whatever good happens to Rasool Ullah is good that is happening to you.

198
00:13:13,302 --> 00:13:15,986
And Rasool Allah ﷺ has given you immunity.

199
00:13:16,433 --> 00:13:17,667
He said: You're lying to me.

200
00:13:17,730 --> 00:13:20,508
he said: This is a sign this is the turban of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

201
00:13:20,671 --> 00:13:22,809
So, Safwaan(صفوان) came back with Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب)

202
00:13:23,224 --> 00:13:25,071
and he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ, and said;

203
00:13:25,383 --> 00:13:29,655
This man is claiming that you forgive me and give me immunity Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes.

204
00:13:30,112 --> 00:13:33,460
Safwaan(صفوان) said: Give me two months to think about it, before becoming Muslim.

205
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:36,161
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: I give you four months.

206
00:13:36,613 --> 00:13:38,439
Safwaan(صفوان) eventually became Muslim.

207
00:13:39,422 --> 00:13:44,951
Rasool Allah ﷺ has destroyed the idols and the Kuffr(كفر) of Makkah.

208
00:13:45,325 --> 00:13:50,840
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to spread the sovereignty of Islam in the surrounding area.

209
00:13:51,194 --> 00:13:55,652
So he sent Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) in Ramadan(رمضان) to Banni Judaimah(بني جذيمة),

210
00:13:56,064 --> 00:13:58,231
 this is an Arab tribe close to Makkah.

211
00:13:58,918 --> 00:14:04,020
It says in Bukhari(بخاريْ), Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to Banni Judaimah(بني جذيمة).

212
00:14:04,075 --> 00:14:05,128
فَدَعَاهُمْ اِلَى الْاِسْلَامْ

213
00:14:05,153 --> 00:14:06,366
He invited them to Islam,

214
00:14:06,405 --> 00:14:08,130
فَلَمْ يُحْسِنُو اَنْ يَقُوْلُوْ اَسْلَمْنَا

215
00:14:08,489 --> 00:14:11,797
They were not educated enough to say we become Muslim but they said;

216
00:14:12,012 --> 00:14:12,826
صَبَاعْنَا

217
00:14:13,436 --> 00:14:17,618
The Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) when somebody would become Muslim

218
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:21,329
they would say, he has become a Sa'bay(صابع).

219
00:14:21,847 --> 00:14:24,792
Sa'bay(صابع) is one of the religions of Jahilliyah(جاهلية)

220
00:14:25,104 --> 00:14:28,775
and it was a derogatory term against anyone, who would become Muslim.

221
00:14:29,127 --> 00:14:31,740
So, they would never say that such and such has become Muslim.

222
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:33,927
They would say such and such Saba'a(صباع).

223
00:14:34,428 --> 00:14:38,737
Now, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) he told them become Muslim, they said: Saba'ana(صباعنا)

224
00:14:39,074 --> 00:14:45,710
In reality, they wanted to be Muslim, but they will not learned enough to know that they should use the term Aslamna(أسلمنا).

225
00:14:46,665 --> 00:14:51,241
They picked up this word that they heard everybody else say and they were repeating it.

226
00:14:51,582 --> 00:14:53,217
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) killed them.

227
00:14:53,631 --> 00:14:56,234
And he captured the rest

228
00:14:56,757 --> 00:15:01,928
and he handed over one prisoner to every soldier of his army.

229
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:07,032
And then Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) gave his instructions to the army

230
00:15:07,721 --> 00:15:11,291
every soldier to execute his prisoner.

231
00:15:11,822 --> 00:15:14,131
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) was in this army and he said;

232
00:15:14,171 --> 00:15:18,111
In the name of Allah, I'm not going to kill my prisoner.

233
00:15:18,338 --> 00:15:22,562
وَلله لَا اَقْتُلْ اَسِيْرِيْ ،وَلَا يَقْتُلْ رَجُلٌ مِنْ اَصْحَابِي اَسِيْرًا

234
00:15:23,307 --> 00:15:29,776
I'm not going to kill my prisoner and none of my companions are going to kill their's.

235
00:15:30,198 --> 00:15:35,546
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) saw that there's this was a clear mistake, on behalf of Khalid(خالد).

236
00:15:35,812 --> 00:15:40,320
 These people have become Muslim and then they were killed, and then they were taken as prisoners.

237
00:15:40,608 --> 00:15:44,605
And now we are told to execute our prisoners, I am not going to do it.

238
00:15:44,950 --> 00:15:50,756
So, it was a clear disobeying of the order of the Ameer(امير) on behalf of Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر).

239
00:15:51,076 --> 00:15:57,171
Now Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) knows the teachings of Islam that you should obey the Umarah(أمراء), follow the Ameer(أمير)

240
00:15:57,442 --> 00:16:04,196
but he also knows that we should only follow the Ameer(أمير), when the Ameer(أمير) gives us an order that is Halal(حلال).

241
00:16:04,436 --> 00:16:07,990
If he tells us to do something that is Haram(حرام) there is no obedience.

242
00:16:08,303 --> 00:16:13,174
And we know an army is that such a thing mutiny is such a dangerous thing to do.

243
00:16:13,479 --> 00:16:16,479
But Abdullah Ibn Umar رضي الله عنه not only did it himself

244
00:16:16,550 --> 00:16:19,409
but he said also all of my companions people, who will listen to me,

245
00:16:19,788 --> 00:16:24,209
the people who came with me, they're not going to kill their prisoners.

246
00:16:24,788 --> 00:16:28,368
So, the issue was raised with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

247
00:16:28,635 --> 00:16:31,604
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) that what you have done is right.

248
00:16:32,092 --> 00:16:38,737
Rasool Allah ﷺ approved Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) in his disobedience to the Ameer(أمير).

249
00:16:39,071 --> 00:16:42,451
 And then Rasool Allah ﷺ raised his hands and said;

250
00:16:42,638 --> 00:16:49,516
اَللَّهُمَ اِنِيْ اَبْرَاءُ اِلَيْكَ مِمَّا صَنْعَ خَالِدْ اَللَّهُمَ اِنِيْ اَبْرَاءُ اِلَيْكَ مِمَّا صَنْعَ خَالِدْ

251
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:54,014
O Allah, I declare that I am free of what Khalid(خالد) has done.

252
00:16:54,299 --> 00:16:58,033
O Allah I declare that I'm innocent of what Khalid(خالد) has done.

253
00:16:58,946 --> 00:17:04,833
Rasool Allah ﷺ made it clear that what Khalid(خالد) has done is wrong.

254
00:17:05,161 --> 00:17:07,603
These people should not have been killed.

255
00:17:08,147 --> 00:17:11,736
And Rasool Allah ﷺ approved, Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) in his action.

256
00:17:11,774 --> 00:17:19,505
 So the first lesson we learn here is that we should not follow Aulea Al Amoor(أولياء الأمور), Walli Ul Amr(ولي الأمر) the people in authority,

257
00:17:19,719 --> 00:17:21,410
when they tell us to do something Haram(حرام).

258
00:17:21,778 --> 00:17:25,555
They are to be disobeyed, if they tell us to do something Haram(حرام).

259
00:17:26,625 --> 00:17:29,611
Another incident that happened with this Sariyyah(سريه),

260
00:17:30,008 --> 00:17:34,934
there was a man among them who didn't really belong to that tribe.

261
00:17:35,727 --> 00:17:41,954
But he was there because the woman whom he loves is from that tribe.

262
00:17:42,451 --> 00:17:44,470
So, that's the only reason why he was there.

263
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:50,646
He was among the people, who were arrested and his hands were tied.

264
00:17:51,231 --> 00:17:55,536
So he told the Muslim soldier, who was guarding him

265
00:17:55,961 --> 00:18:01,281
to just allow me to go and speak, he pointed out towards some women

266
00:18:01,957 --> 00:18:05,846
and he told the Muslim just allow me to go and

267
00:18:06,370 --> 00:18:15,019
have a final visit or final word with those women over there and then do with me whatever you want, just the last sight.

268
00:18:16,048 --> 00:18:18,913
So, the Muslim allowed him, so he went and he said;

269
00:18:18,962 --> 00:18:21,397
اَسْلمِيْ حُبَيْشْ ، قَبْلَنَا نَفَادَ الْعَيْشْ

270
00:18:21,437 --> 00:18:24,135
Aslami(أسلمي) means accept or means become Muslim

271
00:18:24,601 --> 00:18:25,951
Hubeesh(حُبيش), her name.

272
00:18:26,535 --> 00:18:27,674
قَبْلَنَا نَفَادَ الْعَيْشْ

273
00:18:27,741 --> 00:18:29,019
Before life is over.

274
00:18:29,321 --> 00:18:29,686
She said:

275
00:18:29,726 --> 00:18:30,474
 فَدَيْتُكَ

276
00:18:30,514 --> 00:18:32,551
 I would sacrifice myself for you.

277
00:18:32,739 --> 00:18:35,723
And then he was taken and executed.

278
00:18:36,528 --> 00:18:40,927
She saw that and she came over him and sight once or twice

279
00:18:41,157 --> 00:18:43,462
and then she fell next to him dead.

280
00:18:43,844 --> 00:18:46,347
When this story was related to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

281
00:18:46,387 --> 00:18:47,305
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

282
00:18:47,345 --> 00:18:49,215
 اَمَا كَانَ فِيْكُمْ رَجُلٌ رَحِيْمْ

283
00:18:49,506 --> 00:18:51,814
Wasn't there a merciful man among you.

284
00:18:52,576 --> 00:18:58,412
Not only was the killing wrong but also you killed this man in such a way

285
00:18:58,452 --> 00:19:03,318
and Rasool Allah ﷺ felt sorry for these people and what happened to them

286
00:19:03,358 --> 00:19:09,941
and therefore Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه to pay the Diya(دية).

287
00:19:10,454 --> 00:19:18,520
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was sent by Rasool Allah ﷺ to pay Blood Money, compensation for all those who were killed.

288
00:19:18,793 --> 00:19:21,008
Because the ones, who were killed are Muslims

289
00:19:21,591 --> 00:19:26,403
they made a mistake by saying Saba'ana(صباعنا) but in reality what they mean is Aslam'na(أسلمنا).

290
00:19:26,798 --> 00:19:28,076
They were paid for everything.

291
00:19:28,556 --> 00:19:34,675
Anything that was missing, their belongings that were taken Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) compensated them for everything

292
00:19:34,846 --> 00:19:37,666
blood money in addition to any belongings that were taken from them.

293
00:19:37,854 --> 00:19:42,060
And then there was some leftover money with him, he gave it to them just in case.

294
00:19:43,014 --> 00:19:46,240
So, this is how Rasool Allah ﷺ dealt with this situation.

295
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,837
These were Muslims, who are killed by mistake.

296
00:19:49,162 --> 00:19:55,991
They were paid blood money, but pay attention to what Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) has to say after he mentions this incident.

297
00:19:56,063 --> 00:19:56,524
 He said;

298
00:19:56,798 --> 00:20:00,507
فَقَتَلَ طَائِفَةْ كَثِيْرَةْ مِنْهُمْ، وَقَتَلَ اَكْثَرَ الْاَسرَى اَيْضاً

299
00:20:00,997 --> 00:20:01,997
Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) say;

300
00:20:02,267 --> 00:20:02,989
فقتلا,

301
00:20:03,354 --> 00:20:05,275
He killed, meaning Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد),

302
00:20:05,529 --> 00:20:09,189
he killed many of them and he killed most of the prisoners also.

303
00:20:09,692 --> 00:20:12,430
وَمَعَ هَذَا لَمْ يَعْزِلَه’ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

304
00:20:12,787 --> 00:20:18,341
Nevertheless, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not fire him from his position.

305
00:20:18,635 --> 00:20:20,682
 بَلِّ اسْتَمَرَّ بِهِ اَمِيْرًا

306
00:20:21,173 --> 00:20:26,593
But Rasool Allah ﷺ kept on appointing Khalid(خالد) in positions of responsibility as an Ameer(امير).

307
00:20:27,392 --> 00:20:29,807
وَاِنْ كَانَ تَبرا مِنْه’ فِيْ صَنْيِعْهِ ذَالِكْ

308
00:20:29,887 --> 00:20:35,729
Even though Rasool Allah ﷺ announced and declared that he is free and innocent of what Khalid(خالد) has done.

309
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,282
وَوَدَى مَا كَانَ جَنَاه’ خَطَاً فِيْ دَمِّ اَوْ مَالٍ

310
00:20:39,612 --> 00:20:47,074
And Rasool Allah ﷺ paid compensation for the mistakes of Khalid(خالد) that were done in blood or wealth.

311
00:20:47,518 --> 00:20:50,538
فَفِيْهِ دَلِيْلٌ لَاَحَدٍ الْقَوْلَيْنِ بَيْنَ الْعَلَمَاءْ

312
00:20:51,097 --> 00:20:54,725
In this there's evidence for one of the opinion of the scholars.

313
00:20:55,159 --> 00:20:57,678
فِيْ اَنَّ خَطَاَ الْاِمَامْ يَكُوْن فِيْ بَيْتِ الْمَال’

314
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:00,256
That when the Imam(اِمَام) commits a mistake

315
00:21:00,596 --> 00:21:05,708
the money is not paid from his money but from the treasury of the Muslims, Wallah O Alam(والله اعلم).

316
00:21:05,970 --> 00:21:06,634
 And then he says:

317
00:21:06,908 --> 00:21:12,102
وَلِهَذا لَمْ يَعْزِلْه’ اَلصَدِّيق حِيْنَ قَتَلَ مَالِك بِنْ نُوْيْرَةْ اَيَّامً الرِّدَّةْ،

318
00:21:12,283 --> 00:21:17,302
وَتَاَّوَل عَلَيْهِ مَا تَاَّوَّلَ حِيْنَ ضَرَبَ عُنُقَه’ وَاصْطَفى اِمْرَاَتَه’ اُمُ تَمِيْمْ

319
00:21:17,689 --> 00:21:27,220
And that is why Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه did not change him, did not fire him, in the time of riddah(ردة) during the days of Apostasy

320
00:21:27,540 --> 00:21:35,019
and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) excused him, when he killed Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويره), who was supposedly Muslim.

321
00:21:35,236 --> 00:21:38,018
And he took over his wife Umm O Tamim(أم تميم).

322
00:21:38,345 --> 00:21:42,989
And we talked about this in the lecture series of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

323
00:21:43,251 --> 00:21:46,034
that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) killed Malik Bin Nuwairah(مالك بن نويره)

324
00:21:46,454 --> 00:21:49,281
and then he took his wife Umm O Tamim(أم تميم).

325
00:21:49,719 --> 00:21:53,328
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was angry by the actions of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and said;

326
00:21:53,375 --> 00:21:55,333
 اِعْزِلْه’ فَاِنَّ فِيْ سَيْفِه رَهَقاً

327
00:21:55,470 --> 00:21:59,193
Fire him, change him because his sword is severe.

328
00:21:59,548 --> 00:22:03,395
فَقَالَ اَلصِدِيِقْ لَا اَغْمِدُ سَيْفَاً سَلَّهُ الله عَلَى الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ

329
00:22:03,626 --> 00:22:11,746
I am not gonna sheath a sword that was unsheathed by Allahعَزّوجَلّ on the Mushrikeen(مشركين), on the polytheists.

330
00:22:11,985 --> 00:22:18,787
This was a sword drawn by Allahعَزّوجَلّ on the Kuffar(كفار), I'm not gonna put it down.

331
00:22:19,137 --> 00:22:28,822
Therefore we can learn from this Hadd-El-Nabwi(ألحدّ النبوي), the Sunnah(سنة) in dealing with the mistakes of the Muslims in battle.

332
00:22:29,408 --> 00:22:32,146
These were Muslims and they were compensated

333
00:22:33,158 --> 00:22:37,390
They were Muslim and they were compensated for the mistake of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

334
00:22:37,673 --> 00:22:39,664
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was not imprisoned.

335
00:22:40,004 --> 00:22:42,499
He was not fired from his position.

336
00:22:42,745 --> 00:22:45,412
Why Because there is Ta'aweel(تعويل).

337
00:22:45,705 --> 00:22:48,987
He didn't assume them to be Muslim.

338
00:22:49,181 --> 00:22:55,693
But if a leader kills Muslims and he knows that they are Muslim then this is a different situation.

339
00:22:56,110 --> 00:22:57,530
Here the Hukm(حكم) would be different.

340
00:22:58,077 --> 00:22:59,791
The situation we're talking about

341
00:23:00,180 --> 00:23:06,514
is where the issue was clear to people like Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) and the ones with him that these are Muslim.

342
00:23:06,936 --> 00:23:10,785
But with Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), he definitely did not consider them to be Muslim.

343
00:23:10,825 --> 00:23:17,539
I mean, we cannot assume no one should assume that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) ordered Muslims to be executed.

344
00:23:17,643 --> 00:23:19,631
That is impossible! That's not the case.

345
00:23:19,907 --> 00:23:22,380
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) considered them to be Kuffar(كفار).

346
00:23:22,767 --> 00:23:27,816
A Muslim is never handed over to the Kuffar(كفار) and the Muslim is never betrayed

347
00:23:28,330 --> 00:23:29,849
because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

348
00:23:29,905 --> 00:23:33,070
اَلْمُسْلِمْ أَخُ الْمُسْلِمْ، لَا يَظْلِمُه، وَلَا يَخْذِلُه’، وَلَا يَكْذِبُه’، ولا يحقره،

349
00:23:33,565 --> 00:23:36,439
Muslim is the brother of a Muslim, he doesn't give him up,

350
00:23:36,532 --> 00:23:39,775
he doesn't betray him, and he doesn't oppress him.

351
00:23:40,584 --> 00:23:45,902
So the way Rasool Allah ﷺ dealt with this situation is that Rasool Ullah made it clear that he disagrees with it.

352
00:23:46,254 --> 00:23:49,827
But he did not punish Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) for it.

353
00:23:49,923 --> 00:23:54,427
But he paid the blood money to the families of the deceased.

354
00:23:55,330 --> 00:24:02,728
And again, the reason why Rasool Ullah paid them is, because the diseased were Muslim, they weren't even Kafir(كافر).

355
00:24:02,998 --> 00:24:08,052
 And I tried to clarify this ruling because I think there's a lot of confusion surrounding it.

356
00:24:08,548 --> 00:24:14,288
Unfortunately, some Muslims value the blood of Al-Kuffar(الكفار) more than the blood of the Muslims

357
00:24:14,438 --> 00:24:17,647
and they're willing to hand over their Muslim brothers to the Kuffar(كفار)

358
00:24:17,970 --> 00:24:23,796
and they're willing to fight in fact not only hand over to the Kuffar(كفار) but to fight their Muslim brothers

359
00:24:23,868 --> 00:24:29,583
 and this is because the understanding of Wala'a(ولآء) and Bara'a(برآء) in this time is very weak.

360
00:24:29,923 --> 00:24:33,679
This is one aspect of Aqeedah(عقيده) in which the Muslims need to concentrate on

361
00:24:33,844 --> 00:24:38,934
they should know who the loyalty belongs to, and who the Muslim should be free from.

362
00:24:39,242 --> 00:24:44,123
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to destroy Al-Uzzaa(اَلْاُعُزَّةْ).

363
00:24:44,195 --> 00:24:48,833
 Al-Uzzaa(اَلْاُعُزَّةْ) was one of the great gods of the Mushrikeen(مشركين) in those days.

364
00:24:49,314 --> 00:24:56,044
Al-Laat(اَلَّات) wal Uzzaa(اَلْاُعُزَّةْ), Hubal(حُبَل) these are the famous idols that belong to the Mushrikeen(مشركين)

365
00:24:56,084 --> 00:25:00,958
 they held them and they consider them to be among their greatest deities.

366
00:25:01,077 --> 00:25:07,748
 Rasool Allah ﷺ destroyed the false idols, false gods, the idols surrounding Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

367
00:25:07,963 --> 00:25:11,931
And now, Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to destroy Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ), which was outside of Makkah(مكه).

368
00:25:12,407 --> 00:25:16,355
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) went there and the custodians of Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ) ran away.

369
00:25:16,821 --> 00:25:18,842
They didn't fight, they didn't stand to fight.

370
00:25:19,276 --> 00:25:25,614
But in fact the one responsible for Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ) he put the sword around the neck of Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ)

371
00:25:25,654 --> 00:25:30,974
and told Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ) to defend yourself against Khalid(خالد)

372
00:25:31,392 --> 00:25:35,302
and if you don't defend yourself, then you deserve what will happen to you.

373
00:25:35,572 --> 00:25:39,685
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) he came to Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ) and he destroyed it, he destroyed the idol.

374
00:25:40,082 --> 00:25:42,860
When he came back and this narrations is in Al-Bayhaqi(ألْبَيْهَقِيْ).

375
00:25:43,414 --> 00:25:45,148
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: What did he do?

376
00:25:45,181 --> 00:25:46,597
He said: I destroyed Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ).

377
00:25:46,947 --> 00:25:49,900
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: You did nothing. Go back!

378
00:25:50,376 --> 00:25:52,142
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) went back.

379
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:57,259
And now he found a naked woman with her hair was messed up

380
00:25:57,322 --> 00:26:00,009
 and she was throwing dirt on herself and she was yelling

381
00:26:00,427 --> 00:26:04,036
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) put her to the sword and killed her.

382
00:26:04,564 --> 00:26:06,616
And then when he went back to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

383
00:26:06,696 --> 00:26:09,048
Rasool Ullah told him: What did you do?

384
00:26:09,220 --> 00:26:13,364
He said: I found a naked woman and I executed her.

385
00:26:13,642 --> 00:26:17,880
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: That is Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ), you have killed her.

386
00:26:18,611 --> 00:26:21,489
So, Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ) was some type of Jin(جن) or Shaytan(شيطان)

387
00:26:22,158 --> 00:26:26,001
it was an idol from the outside, but there was a Jin(جن) living inside it

388
00:26:26,251 --> 00:26:31,467
or Shaytan(شيطان) living inside it, and that Shaytan(شيطان) came out, in the form of this naked woman,

389
00:26:31,689 --> 00:26:35,597
so when Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), executed her that was the end of Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ).

390
00:26:35,804 --> 00:26:39,089
 Therefore, there was some superstition attached to Al-Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ)

391
00:26:39,161 --> 00:26:43,036
 because there was this, living spirit in it, this Shaytan(شيطان) or Jin(جن).

392
00:26:43,423 --> 00:26:46,282
Probably that played a role in the deceiving of the people.

393
00:26:46,863 --> 00:26:50,301
Rasool Allah ﷺ has said: That there will be no more Uzzaa(اَلْعُزَّةْ) after this day.

394
00:26:50,814 --> 00:26:53,255
Some of the Ihkaam(احكام) in Fath Makkah(فتح مكه),

395
00:26:53,626 --> 00:26:57,239
Rasool Allah ﷺ stayed 18 days and in one narration 19 days.

396
00:26:57,548 --> 00:27:02,235
And during this period he would not fast and he would shorten the Salah(صلاة).

397
00:27:02,302 --> 00:27:06,505
 Therefore for example, in the Shafie Mad'hab(شافعي مذهب) and some of the other scholars,

398
00:27:06,766 --> 00:27:15,845
they have taken from this, the ruling that the traveler can shorten the salah(صلاة) and break the fast for 18 days

399
00:27:15,980 --> 00:27:18,083
 because of this narration that is in Bukhari(بخاري).

400
00:27:18,345 --> 00:27:20,383
Obviously, there's a difference of opinion.

401
00:27:20,591 --> 00:27:23,880
 Some of them say three days and here 18 days.

402
00:27:24,127 --> 00:27:26,470
And then you have even Ibn Taymiya(اِبن تَيْمِيَه) For example, he says;

403
00:27:26,657 --> 00:27:33,241
As long as you are customarily considered to be a traveler you can break your fast, and shorten the Salah(صلاة).

404
00:27:34,027 --> 00:27:41,560
 Then there was another incident, and this is the incident of the woman from Bani Makhzoom(بني مخذوم), who was caught stealing.

405
00:27:42,129 --> 00:27:49,423
And Bannu Makhzoom(بنو مخذوم) are prominent family in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), family of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) among the leaders of the society.

406
00:27:49,899 --> 00:27:57,380
 And one of these, and a member of this clan and a noble woman committed the Hadd(حد) of stealing.

407
00:27:57,767 --> 00:28:04,694
So Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that the punishment of cutting the hand, be applied to her.

408
00:28:05,573 --> 00:28:09,702
Her people and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) they were very concerned about this.

409
00:28:10,266 --> 00:28:16,706
They're used to the fact that the weak the slaves the people who don't have protection they are punished.

410
00:28:17,143 --> 00:28:20,036
 But if you belong to the nobility then there's ways out

411
00:28:20,533 --> 00:28:23,463
we can sort out the deal, find the way out for her.

412
00:28:23,860 --> 00:28:27,943
 So they wanted to appeal the punishment.

413
00:28:28,798 --> 00:28:32,693
So, they wanted somebody to speak to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

414
00:28:33,345 --> 00:28:40,975
and the person whom they chose was the son of Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه), Usama رضي الله عنه.

415
00:28:41,316 --> 00:28:45,816
They knew that Usama bin Zaid رضي الله عنه is very close to Rasool Ullah.

416
00:28:46,110 --> 00:28:47,887
Rasool Allah ﷺ used to love his father

417
00:28:47,927 --> 00:28:55,758
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ loved Usama(اُسَامَه) greatly after his father Zaid Bin Harisa(زيد بن حارثه) was a Shaheed(شهيد) in the Battle of Mu'tah(مَؤتَة).

418
00:28:56,283 --> 00:29:00,218
So because of the strong relationship between Rasool Allah ﷺ and Usama bin Zaid(اُسَامَه بن زيد),

419
00:29:00,599 --> 00:29:03,036
they chose him to speak to Rasool Ullah.

420
00:29:03,564 --> 00:29:06,910
Usama bin Zaid(اُسَامَه بن زيد) agreed and he spoke to Rasool Ullah about it

421
00:29:07,017 --> 00:29:08,470
the face of Rasool Allah changed,

422
00:29:08,564 --> 00:29:13,352
تَلَوَّنَ وَجْهَ رَسول الله صلى الله علي وسلم وَقَالَ: اَتُكَلِّمُنِيْ فِيْ حَدٍ مِنْ حَدُوْدِ الله

423
00:29:13,486 --> 00:29:18,458
You speak to me in a Hadd(حدّ) in a punishment from among the punishments of Allah.

424
00:29:18,627 --> 00:29:19,306
Usama(اُسَامَه) said;

425
00:29:19,346 --> 00:29:20,599
 إستغفرلي يا رسول الله

426
00:29:20,639 --> 00:29:22,814
O Rasool Ullah seek my forgiveness

427
00:29:23,083 --> 00:29:29,875
and that day Rasool Allah ﷺ stood and gave a Khut'ba(خطبه) and he said, After praising Allah

428
00:29:30,205 --> 00:29:35,490
فَاِنَّمَا اَهْلَكَ النَّاس قَبْلِكُم اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْ اِذَا سَرَقَ فِيْهِمْ الشَّرِيْف تَرَكُوْا

429
00:29:35,783 --> 00:29:38,907
وَاِذَا سَرَقَ فِيْهِمْ اَلضَّعِيْفْ اَقَامُوا عَلَيْهَ الْحَدْ

430
00:29:39,286 --> 00:29:43,565
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: The thing that destroyed people before you,

431
00:29:43,752 --> 00:29:48,752
is that when the noble man among them would steal, they would leave him

432
00:29:49,127 --> 00:29:51,661
and when the weak among them steals.

433
00:29:51,923 --> 00:29:54,688
They would establish the punishment against them.

434
00:29:55,017 --> 00:30:01,880
وَالَّذِى نَفْسٌ محمد بِيَدِه لَوْ اَنَّ فَاطِمَةَ بِنْت محمد سَرَقَتْ لَقَطَعْتُ يَدَهَا

435
00:30:02,377 --> 00:30:05,318
In the name of Whom, my soul is in His Hands

436
00:30:05,767 --> 00:30:09,755
if Fatima(فاطمه) the daughter of Muhammad(محمد) would steal, I would cut her hand.

437
00:30:10,502 --> 00:30:14,036
ثُمَّ اَمَرَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم بِتِلْكَ الْمَرَاَةَ فَقُطِعَتْ يَدُهَا

438
00:30:14,330 --> 00:30:17,470
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that the hand of that woman be cut

439
00:30:17,658 --> 00:30:19,286
and it says in the Hadith(حديث).

440
00:30:19,752 --> 00:30:21,008
فَحَسُنَتْ تَوْبَتُهَا

441
00:30:21,061 --> 00:30:23,624
She repented after that and she got married.

442
00:30:23,829 --> 00:30:24,796
And Ayesha(عائشه) would say;

443
00:30:24,892 --> 00:30:28,333
فَكَانَتْ تَاْتِيْ بَعْدَ ذَالِكَ فَاَرْفَعَ حَاجَتَهَا اِلَى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

444
00:30:28,475 --> 00:30:31,905
She would visit me after that, if she needs something from Rasool Ullah,

445
00:30:32,127 --> 00:30:34,423
and I would speak to Rasool Allah ﷺ on her behalf.

446
00:30:35,177 --> 00:30:41,755
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling us, a law that governs the life of men.

447
00:30:42,236 --> 00:30:47,130
If in a particular society, there's a double standard in applying justice,

448
00:30:47,439 --> 00:30:52,333
where the weak are punished, while the strong are spared,

449
00:30:52,673 --> 00:30:55,423
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will destroy such a society.

450
00:30:55,616 --> 00:31:00,911
 Nowadays, brothers and sisters, not only do we have a double standard in applying the law of Allah,

451
00:31:01,220 --> 00:31:03,381
we don't have the law of Allah all together.

452
00:31:03,770 --> 00:31:10,454
So, if Allah would destroy a society and take away the Barakah(بركة) from such as society take away the blessing from it,

453
00:31:11,001 --> 00:31:14,248
just because they have a double standard in applying the law of Allah.

454
00:31:14,502 --> 00:31:16,661
What do you think will happen to us now

455
00:31:16,876 --> 00:31:19,048
because we don't have law of Allah all together.

456
00:31:19,157 --> 00:31:20,427
There's a Hadith(حديث) that says

457
00:31:20,611 --> 00:31:23,204
that applying one Hadd(حدّ), of the Hadood(حدود) of Allah,

458
00:31:23,283 --> 00:31:25,921
Hadd(حدّ) is the criminal law in Islam,

459
00:31:26,093 --> 00:31:31,273
One Hadd(حدّ), applying one Hadd(حدّ) is better than 40 days of rain,

460
00:31:31,630 --> 00:31:37,255
there's more blessing in applying the Hadood(حدود) of Allah then rain for 40 days,

461
00:31:37,611 --> 00:31:39,511
how much Barakah(بركة) are we missing now.

462
00:31:39,749 --> 00:31:42,305
And that is why our life is messed up.

463
00:31:42,595 --> 00:31:50,026
We have a lot of resources, we have wealth, we have such a wide expanse of land, look at how large the Muslim world is.

464
00:31:50,330 --> 00:31:51,828
But there's no Barakah(بركة) in the life,

465
00:31:51,868 --> 00:31:54,829
that is because we don't have the Hadood(حدود) of Allah applied.

466
00:31:55,243 --> 00:31:59,564
And we never tasted the blessing of living under an Islamic system to compare.

467
00:31:59,604 --> 00:32:00,478
 See, that's the problem.

468
00:32:00,595 --> 00:32:04,223
But for those who did experience Jahilliyah(جاهلية) and Islam, for example;

469
00:32:04,438 --> 00:32:08,730
There was an Old Woman Who ran into Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

470
00:32:08,770 --> 00:32:12,286
when he was Khalifah(خليفه), and she told him, how long will this affair last.

471
00:32:12,342 --> 00:32:18,159
 I mean, she's talking about the great life that they're living in under Islamic law.

472
00:32:18,421 --> 00:32:21,189
So she asked Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and told him how long will this last.

473
00:32:21,579 --> 00:32:22,580
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) told her;

474
00:32:22,692 --> 00:32:24,454
 مَسْتَقَامَتْ عَلَيْهَا اَمَّتُكُمْ

475
00:32:24,564 --> 00:32:26,533
As long as your leaders follow it.

476
00:32:26,892 --> 00:32:30,542
As long as the leaders are following Al-Haqq(اَلْحَقْ), you're going to enjoy the blessings.

477
00:32:30,767 --> 00:32:33,486
And then this woman is a Bedouin, she doesn't have knowledge.

478
00:32:33,767 --> 00:32:36,224
So, she told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), and who are these Aimmah(آئِمَّه),

479
00:32:36,533 --> 00:32:39,380
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) told her; They are the leaders among you.

480
00:32:40,470 --> 00:32:44,833
So, dear brothers and sisters, we should all make it an objective of ours

481
00:32:45,183 --> 00:32:48,856
to try to establish the law of Allahعَزّوجَلّ on Earth.

482
00:32:49,235 --> 00:32:52,673
To try to establish the Islamic system, to try to establish Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

483
00:32:52,998 --> 00:32:55,235
this is a responsibility on every Muslim.

484
00:32:55,371 --> 00:32:59,252
We want to live the blessing of the Islamic system.

485
00:33:00,014 --> 00:33:04,221
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: After the conquest of Makkah,

486
00:33:04,522 --> 00:33:06,856
لَا هِجْرَةَ  وَلَكِنْ جِهَادْ وَنِيَّةْ

487
00:33:07,764 --> 00:33:11,314
Before the conquest of Makkah, Hijrah(هجرة) was mandatory

488
00:33:12,061 --> 00:33:14,822
it was one of the most important things Muslim should do.

489
00:33:15,172 --> 00:33:20,398
Anybody who becomes Muslim should make Hijrah(هجرة) from Makkah to Madina, or from any other parts of Arabia.

490
00:33:20,884 --> 00:33:23,971
They are in and they should immigrate to Madina.

491
00:33:24,496 --> 00:33:29,842
After Makkah, People would come to Rasool Allah ﷺ and want to make a Hijrah(هجرة),

492
00:33:30,147 --> 00:33:33,001
Rasool Allah ﷺ would tell them that there's no more Hijrah(هجرة), Khalas(خلاص).

493
00:33:33,103 --> 00:33:36,424
The Hijrah(هجرة) is over and the people who did it, received the Ajr(أجْر).

494
00:33:36,800 --> 00:33:38,233
It's now too late to do Hijrah(هجرة).

495
00:33:38,455 --> 00:33:40,789
But now, you are replaced with Jihad(جهاد),

496
00:33:40,892 --> 00:33:46,869
 the thing that takes place of Hijrah(هجرة), and the Ajr(أجْر) of Hijrah(هجرة) is Jihad Fee Sabeel-Lillah(جهاد في سبيل الله).

497
00:33:46,909 --> 00:33:48,790
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says in Bukhari(بخاريْ);

498
00:33:48,962 --> 00:33:53,494
 لَا هِجْرَةَ  وَلَكِنْ جِهَادْ وَنِيَّةْ وَاِذَا اسْتُنْفِرْتُمْ فَانْفِرُوْا

499
00:33:53,879 --> 00:33:57,005
There is no more Hijrah(هجرة) but Jihad(جهاد) had and intention.

500
00:33:57,595 --> 00:34:01,515
And if you are called to fight then you should respond.

501
00:34:02,621 --> 00:34:09,384
 Another man came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he wanted to give a Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Rasool Allah ﷺ to make Hijrah(هجرة).

502
00:34:09,585 --> 00:34:10,715
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

503
00:34:10,811 --> 00:34:12,896
اُبَايِعُه’ عَلى الاِسْلام والْجِهَادْ

504
00:34:13,298 --> 00:34:17,955
 I will take Baiyah(بَيْعة) from him on Islam and Jihad(جهاد) there's no more Hijrah(هجرة).

505
00:34:18,247 --> 00:34:25,088
So, the rule that applies after the conquest of Makkah is Islam and Jihad Fee Sabeel-Lillah(جهاد في سبيل الله).

506
00:34:25,580 --> 00:34:29,447
And Atta Bin Rabah(عطاء بن رباح) one of the Tabieen(تابعين), he said: I visited Ayesha(عائشه)

507
00:34:29,861 --> 00:34:32,648
and we asked her about Hijrah(هجرة), she said:

508
00:34:32,803 --> 00:34:38,625
لَا هِجْرَةَ الْيَوْم، كَانَ الْمُؤمِنُ يَفِرُّ اَحَدَهُمْ بِدِيْنِهِ اِلَى الله ، عَزُّوجَل، وَاِلَى رَسُوْلِه صلى الله عليه وسلم

509
00:34:38,779 --> 00:34:43,130
مَخَافَةَ اَنْ يُفْتَنَ عَلَيْهِ فَاَمَا الْيَوْم فَقَدْ اَظْهَرَ الله الْاِسْلَامَ ،

510
00:34:43,454 --> 00:34:47,713
فَاْلْمُؤمِنُ يَعْبُدُ رَبَّه’ حَيْثُ يَشَاءْ ، وَلَكِنْ جِهَادٌ وَنِيَّةْ

511
00:34:48,206 --> 00:34:49,949
We asked Ayesha(عائشه) about Hijrah(هجرة) she said;

512
00:34:50,147 --> 00:34:51,605
There's no more Hijrah(هجرة) now.

513
00:34:52,053 --> 00:35:01,452
The believer used to flee with, his religion to Allah and to the Messenger of Allah because of fear of going through Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

514
00:35:02,063 --> 00:35:04,106
They would fear that they would lose their religion

515
00:35:04,522 --> 00:35:05,294
فَاَمَّا الْيَوْم

516
00:35:05,334 --> 00:35:08,598
but today, Allahعَزّوجَلّ has made Islam prevalent.

517
00:35:09,053 --> 00:35:12,137
So the believer can worship Allah wherever, he wants,

518
00:35:12,412 --> 00:35:16,656
but you should fight Jihad Fee Sabeel-Lillah(جهاد في سبيل الله) and you should have the intentions to do so.

519
00:35:16,787 --> 00:35:18,642
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) comments on this and says;

520
00:35:18,987 --> 00:35:23,775
فَلَمْ تَبْقَ الْهِجْرَةْ، الَّلهُمَّ اِلَّا اَنْ يَعْرَضَ حَالٌ يَقْتَضِي الْهِجْرَةَ بِسَبَبْ

521
00:35:24,066 --> 00:35:28,208
مُجَاوَرَةِ اَهْلَ الْحَرْبِ ، وَعَدَمَ الْقُدْرَةَ عَلَى اِظْهَارِ الدِّيْنِ عِنْدَهُمْ ،

522
00:35:28,559 --> 00:35:33,389
فَتَجِبُ الْهِجْرَةَ اِلَى دَارِ الْاِسْلَام، وَهَذَا مِمَّا لَا خِلَافَ عليْهِ بَيْنَ الْعُلَمَاءْ

523
00:35:33,715 --> 00:35:35,926
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says; So, there's no more Hijrah(هجرة)

524
00:35:36,052 --> 00:35:41,539
 except, if there are circumstances that necessitate Hijrah(هجرة),

525
00:35:42,112 --> 00:35:46,487
because of being close to the people of Harb(حرب), the people of war the Kuffar(كفار).

526
00:35:46,788 --> 00:35:52,607
And the inability to show the religion among them,

527
00:35:53,044 --> 00:35:58,173
 in this situation, Hijrah(هجرة) becomes mandatory to the land of Islam.

528
00:35:58,387 --> 00:36:02,086
 And this is something that is agreed upon among the scholars.

529
00:36:02,173 --> 00:36:04,281
 So Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says; There's more no more Hijrah(هجرة),

530
00:36:04,593 --> 00:36:10,283
except if we run into a situation that is similar to the situation of the Muslims back then,

531
00:36:10,492 --> 00:36:12,587
then Hijrah(هجرة) would be necessary.

532
00:36:12,737 --> 00:36:17,878
And he gives us the clarification of what he means and that is living among the Kuffar(كفار).

533
00:36:18,315 --> 00:36:21,102
If a person is not able to show his religion

534
00:36:21,178 --> 00:36:25,098
if a person can declare his religion publicly,

535
00:36:25,384 --> 00:36:29,169
not only the aspects that are individually practiced,

536
00:36:29,224 --> 00:36:33,992
 but he can declare all aspects of Islam in this case Hijrah(هجرة) is not mandatory.

537
00:36:34,145 --> 00:36:42,708
But if a person cannot worship Allah as he should then he must make a Hijrah(هجرة) to the land where he can worship Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

538
00:36:43,209 --> 00:36:47,585
Nowadays, we do have clear land of Kuffr(كفر) and clear land of Harb(حرب),

539
00:36:48,065 --> 00:36:50,590
but we do not have a clear land of Islam.

540
00:36:50,772 --> 00:36:53,201
Therefore, the rule that applies now

541
00:36:53,391 --> 00:36:58,656
is that the Muslim should make Hijrah(هجرة) to the place where they can worship Allah the best.

542
00:36:59,074 --> 00:37:01,148
So, it's a relative issue a Muslim,

543
00:37:01,274 --> 00:37:08,964
if he is living in a particular place and he is able to worship Allah as he should then he can remain there

544
00:37:09,004 --> 00:37:15,036
but if he's not, then he should search for the place where there's the least fear on his Deen(دِيْن),

545
00:37:15,170 --> 00:37:16,853
not his Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) his Deen(دِيْن),

546
00:37:17,099 --> 00:37:19,266
and he should make Hijrah(هجرة) to that place.

547
00:37:19,290 --> 00:37:22,017
The final Hadith(حديث) in this section

548
00:37:22,072 --> 00:37:28,301
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) mentions this Hadith(حديث) as the closing of the chapter of Fath-E-Makkah(فتح مكه).

549
00:37:28,625 --> 00:37:32,707
This Hadith(حديث), it talks about Amr Bin Salamah رضي الله عنه.

550
00:37:32,857 --> 00:37:36,947
Amr Bin Salamah(عَمرُو بن سلمه) was not from Makkah, he belonged to another tribe.

551
00:37:37,363 --> 00:37:40,233
And he describes the situation back then, he says;

552
00:37:40,488 --> 00:37:48,398
Whenever the travelers would travel by, we would ask them about this man referring to Muhammadﷺ,

553
00:37:48,561 --> 00:37:54,148
وَكَانَ يَمُرُّ بِنَا الرُكْبَانْ فَنَسْاَلُهُمْ: مَا لِلنَّاسِ مَاِللنَّاسِ؟ مَا هَذَاالرَّجُلْ؟

554
00:37:54,615 --> 00:37:56,509
We would ask them, about this man.

555
00:37:56,549 --> 00:37:59,382
So the news about Muhammadﷺ was all over Arabia.

556
00:38:00,228 --> 00:38:02,469
And it was the news of the day.

557
00:38:02,691 --> 00:38:08,175
So, people would ask the travelers about any new news about Muhammadﷺ,

558
00:38:08,215 --> 00:38:11,349
that was the major event, the Daw'ah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

559
00:38:11,611 --> 00:38:13,325
So, it was not an obscure Daw'ah(دعوة).

560
00:38:13,483 --> 00:38:17,325
It was the breaking news for the people all over.

561
00:38:17,728 --> 00:38:18,892
So, Amr Bin Salamah(عَمرُو بن سلمه) said;

562
00:38:19,052 --> 00:38:24,392
We would ask the travelers about this man, and they would say;

563
00:38:24,469 --> 00:38:29,900
فَيَقُوْلُوْنْ: يَزْعَمُ اَنَّ الله اَرْسَلَه’ وَاَوْحَى اِلَيْهِ أو أوحى الله بِكَذَا

564
00:38:30,462 --> 00:38:37,073
So, they would say he claims that Allah has sent him and he's receiving revelation.

565
00:38:37,298 --> 00:38:40,407
And he just received the revelation of this and that.

566
00:38:40,534 --> 00:38:46,504
So these travelers would mentioned some of the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an, they're up to date.

567
00:38:47,115 --> 00:38:49,057
So, they would mention these Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an,

568
00:38:49,114 --> 00:38:51,185
Amr Bin Salamah(عَمرُو بن سلمه) was a child at that time,

569
00:38:51,452 --> 00:38:55,501
and he would hear this dialogue, he would hear this conversation

570
00:38:55,879 --> 00:38:59,291
and he would remember those Ayaat(آيات), he would memorize the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an.

571
00:38:59,745 --> 00:39:01,848
Even though his people were Kuffar(كفار) at that time,

572
00:39:01,935 --> 00:39:06,918
but the people were carrying the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an around even though they were Kuffar(كفار),

573
00:39:07,220 --> 00:39:11,713
but it was the news for them Rasool Ullah receive this, Rasool Allah ﷺ received that.

574
00:39:12,676 --> 00:39:14,356
فَكُنْتُ اَحْفَظْ ذَالِكَ الْكَلَامْ

575
00:39:14,396 --> 00:39:16,201
I used to memorize those words.

576
00:39:16,465 --> 00:39:18,992
فَكَاَنَّمَا يَقر فِي صَدْرِيْ

577
00:39:19,147 --> 00:39:22,206
As if they would stay inside my breast,

578
00:39:22,597 --> 00:39:26,648
these words, the words of Qur'an would just enter into his breast and stay there.

579
00:39:27,532 --> 00:39:30,639
وَكَانَتِ الْعَرَبْ تَلَوَمُ بِاِسْلَامِهِمْ الْفَتْحْ،

580
00:39:30,918 --> 00:39:35,750
The Arabs were waiting for the conquest, before becoming Muslim.

581
00:39:35,951 --> 00:39:37,136
The Arabs were watching.

582
00:39:37,318 --> 00:39:43,536
They saw two parties in this conflict, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) on one side and Muhammadﷺ on the other.

583
00:39:43,873 --> 00:39:46,503
And they were waiting to see the result.

584
00:39:47,431 --> 00:39:49,868
 That is the situation with many people.

585
00:39:50,734 --> 00:39:55,489
They do not search for the truth, but they look at who is more victorious,

586
00:39:55,814 --> 00:40:00,072
they look at who is more victorious and they follow that victorious party.

587
00:40:00,396 --> 00:40:03,393
 وَكَانَتِ الْعَرَبْ تَلَوَمُ بِاِسْلَامِهِمْ الْفَتْحْ،

588
00:40:04,004 --> 00:40:06,353
 They were waiting to see who would win.

589
00:40:06,726 --> 00:40:08,545
 So, they would say;

590
00:40:08,613 --> 00:40:13,354
فَيَقُوْلُوْنْ: اَتْرَكُوْه’ وَقَوْمَه’، فَاِنَّه’ اِنْ ظَهَرَ عَلَيْهِمْ فَهُوَ نَبِيٌ صَادِقْ

591
00:40:14,064 --> 00:40:19,105
And they would say: If he wins against his people,

592
00:40:19,145 --> 00:40:20,723
they would say: Leave him and his people alone.

593
00:40:20,957 --> 00:40:24,851
If he defeats is people, then he is a Nabi(نَبِي) and he is truthful.

594
00:40:25,084 --> 00:40:30,390
And by the way this is not a correct attitude towards the Daw'ah(دعوة) of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

595
00:40:30,799 --> 00:40:32,493
But that is what the people used to say;

596
00:40:32,747 --> 00:40:37,493
I mean we know from the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, that there are some Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء),

597
00:40:37,831 --> 00:40:40,612
who didn't have any followers, does that make them wrong. No!

598
00:40:41,047 --> 00:40:43,080
I mean, we know the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

599
00:40:43,300 --> 00:40:46,139
on the day of judgment, there will be a Nabi(نَبِي) with 10,

600
00:40:46,179 --> 00:40:47,527
 there will be a Nabi(نَبِي) with five,

601
00:40:47,567 --> 00:40:48,910
there will be Nabi(نَبِي) with three,

602
00:40:49,120 --> 00:40:51,482
there would be Nabi(نَبِي) with two, there would be a Nabi(نَبِي) with one follower

603
00:40:51,572 --> 00:40:54,983
and there would be a Nabi(نَبِي) without any followers all together,

604
00:40:55,462 --> 00:40:58,445
that does not make their Da'wah(دعوة), a failure.

605
00:40:58,782 --> 00:41:01,960
It doesn't mean that they know how to do Da'wah(دعوة), No.

606
00:41:02,293 --> 00:41:04,222
because Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

607
00:41:04,262 --> 00:41:07,794
 إِنَّكَ لَا تَهْدِي مَنْ أَحْبَبْتَ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشَاءُ ۚ

608
00:41:07,988 --> 00:41:11,544
You do not guide whomever you want, but it is Allah, Who guides.

609
00:41:12,167 --> 00:41:15,762
So, the fact that a Nabi(نَبِي) didn't have any followers, that was the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah,

610
00:41:15,802 --> 00:41:20,422
 but he did his job fully in conveying the message.

611
00:41:20,996 --> 00:41:26,465
Anyway, so they waited until Rasool Allah ﷺ defeated his people, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

612
00:41:26,505 --> 00:41:29,824
 Now, obviously the ones, who became Muslim earlier,

613
00:41:30,071 --> 00:41:32,729
the ones who accepted Islam earlier,

614
00:41:32,936 --> 00:41:35,593
they searched for the truth and they found it and they accepted Islam.

615
00:41:35,998 --> 00:41:45,907
Their Ajr(أجْر) and their level in the eyes of Allah is much higher than the ones who became Muslim after the victories of Islam (were becoming very clear),

616
00:41:46,066 --> 00:41:52,436
 and that's why it says in Qur'an that the ones who fight Jihad Fee Sabeel-Lillah(جهاد في سبيل الله)  and spend before the conquest,

617
00:41:52,828 --> 00:42:01,398
 are better and higher in status, than the ones who became Muslim after that, and spent and fought Fee Sabeel-Lillah(في سبيل الله).

618
00:42:01,723 --> 00:42:07,122
 So, there's a difference between becoming Muslim before conquest, and the ones who became Muslim after.

619
00:42:07,162 --> 00:42:12,494
Anyway Amr Bin Salamah رضي الله عنه said that when Rasool Allah ﷺ opened Makkah,

620
00:42:12,909 --> 00:42:15,037
بَادَرَ كُلَّ قَوْمٍ بِاِسْلَامِهِمْ

621
00:42:15,120 --> 00:42:18,995
Every tribe was rushing to become Muslim

622
00:42:19,238 --> 00:42:20,636
وَبَدَرَ اَبِيْ قَوْمِيْ بِاِسْلَامِهِمْ

623
00:42:20,676 --> 00:42:23,367
And my father became Muslim before my people

624
00:42:23,626 --> 00:42:24,550
فَلَمَّا قَدَمْ

625
00:42:24,590 --> 00:42:25,920
When he came back, he said;

626
00:42:26,152 --> 00:42:28,627
جِئْتُكُمْ وَاللهِ مِنْ عِنْدَ نَّبِيْ حَقًا

627
00:42:28,977 --> 00:42:33,692
I came to you in the name of Allah from the Nabi ﷺ,

628
00:42:33,978 --> 00:42:34,647
حقًا

629
00:42:34,867 --> 00:42:36,934
He is truly a Prophet of Allah.

630
00:42:37,168 --> 00:42:37,851
فَقَالْ

631
00:42:37,938 --> 00:42:40,168
he told us, to pray,

632
00:42:40,295 --> 00:42:44,398
صَلُّوْ صَلَاةَ كَذَافِيْ حِيْنَ كَذَا وَصَلُوْ صَلَاةَ كَذَا فِيْ حِيْنَ كَذَا ،

633
00:42:45,084 --> 00:42:48,666
And he told us to pray this Salah(صلاة) at that time and this Salah(صلاة) at that time.

634
00:42:48,795 --> 00:42:54,352
So Rasool Allah ﷺ gave the father of Amr Bin Salamah(عَمرُو بن سلمه) instructions on how to pray.

635
00:42:54,942 --> 00:43:00,867
فَاِذَا حَضَرَتِ الصَّلَاةْ فَلْيُؤَذِّنْ اَحَدكُمْ، وَلَيؤُمَّكُمْ اَكْثَرَكُمْ قُرْآنَا

636
00:43:01,269 --> 00:43:05,311
So when the time of Salah(صلاة) approaches then one of you should make Adhan(آذَان)

637
00:43:05,683 --> 00:43:10,811
and the one, who should be your Imam(اِمَام) is the one who knows the most Qur'an among you.

638
00:43:11,777 --> 00:43:15,958
فَنَظَرُوْ افَلَمْ يَكُنْ اَحَدٌ اَكْثَرْ قُرْآنًا مِّنِّي

639
00:43:16,217 --> 00:43:20,684
So, they searched and they found out that no one knew more Qur'an than me.

640
00:43:21,243 --> 00:43:23,301
لِمَا كُنْتُ اَتَلَقَّى مِنَّ الرُّكْبَاْن

641
00:43:23,405 --> 00:43:25,567
Because of what I learned from the travelers.

642
00:43:25,930 --> 00:43:27,637
فَقَدَّمُوْنِيْ بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ

643
00:43:27,973 --> 00:43:30,195
They made me, their Imam(إمام)

644
00:43:30,275 --> 00:43:33,376
 وَاَنَا ابْنُ سِتٍ اَوْ سَبْعِ سِنِيْنَ،

645
00:43:33,638 --> 00:43:39,130
And I was six years old or seven years old at the time and he became the Imam(اِمَام).

646
00:43:39,954 --> 00:43:43,379
He knew, the most Qur'an among them.

647
00:43:43,760 --> 00:43:44,872
Amr Bin Salamah(عَمرُو بن سلمه) said;

648
00:43:45,019 --> 00:43:49,963
وَكَانَتْ عَلَيَّ بُرْدَةٌ اِذَا سَجَدْتَ تَقَلَّصَتْ عَنِّيْ

649
00:43:50,984 --> 00:43:54,198
He said: I would lead them in Salah(صلاة) and I was wearing a Burdah(بردة),

650
00:43:54,238 --> 00:43:57,214
a Burdah(بردة) is a square garment and

651
00:43:57,486 --> 00:44:00,041
وَكُنْتُ اِذَا سَجَدْتَ تَقَلَّصَتْ عَنِّيْ

652
00:44:00,572 --> 00:44:06,715
When I would make Sujood(سجود), it was too short, this garment that Amr Bin Salamah(عَمرُو بن سلمه) was wearing was too short,

653
00:44:07,254 --> 00:44:14,458
so when he would go in Sujood(سجود), what happen is this garment would rise and his behind would show.

654
00:44:14,897 --> 00:44:19,508
فَقَالَتِ امْرَاَةْ مِنَ الْحَيّْ اَلَا تُغَطُّوْنَ عَنَّا اسْتَ قارِئِكُمْ

655
00:44:19,858 --> 00:44:21,631
So, one woman stood up and said;

656
00:44:21,802 --> 00:44:27,284
Wouldn't you, cover from us, the butt of your, O reciter.

657
00:44:27,693 --> 00:44:33,281
So, when she did make that statement that embarrassing statement against Amr Bin Salamah(عَمرُو بن سلمه).

658
00:44:33,451 --> 00:44:35,171
In fact, in another narration, it says;

659
00:44:35,561 --> 00:44:40,903
فَكُنْتُ اَؤمَّهُمْ فِيْ بَرْدَةْ مَوْصُوْلَة فيفتق فَكُنْتُ اِذَا سَجَدْتْ خَرَجَتْ إستيْ

660
00:44:41,042 --> 00:44:50,002
He said: I used to lead them in Salah(صلاة) in a Bardah(بردة), in a Thoub(ثوب) that had a big tear from behind.

661
00:44:50,158 --> 00:44:53,804
So, when I would make Sujood(سجود) my butt would stick out of that, tear

662
00:44:54,077 --> 00:44:57,379
and that's why this woman made that statement against him and said,

663
00:44:57,762 --> 00:45:01,410
in front of everyone, this was Ya'ani(يعني) in front of everybody, she said;

664
00:45:01,642 --> 00:45:04,976
Cover from us the butt of your, reciter.

665
00:45:05,404 --> 00:45:06,688
So, Amr Bin Salamah(عَمرُو بن سلمه) said;

666
00:45:06,811 --> 00:45:11,625
فَقَطَعُوْا لِيْ قَمِيْصًا، فَمَا فَرِحْتُ بِشَيْءٍ فَرَحِيْ بِذَالِكَ الْقَمِيْصْ

667
00:45:11,757 --> 00:45:15,929
Now, the Imam(اِمَام) said: They bought for me, a Thoub(ثوب),

668
00:45:16,199 --> 00:45:18,477
 now Subhan Allah(سبحان الله) the Imam(اِمَام) has a new Thoub(ثوب)

669
00:45:18,777 --> 00:45:21,786
he's very happy with it. And this is what he said, he said;

670
00:45:22,059 --> 00:45:26,278
And nothing had ever made me so happy as that shirt did.

671
00:45:26,955 --> 00:45:32,497
He was so happy with the new Thoub(ثوب) that, they bought him as an Imam(اِمَام) to cover him up in a Salah(صلاة).

672
00:45:33,195 --> 00:45:34,846
To cover up his Aurah(عَوْرَة).

673
00:45:35,119 --> 00:45:39,278
This is the end of the Ghazwa(غزوة) of Fath Makkah(فتح مكه),

674
00:45:39,402 --> 00:45:42,635
by the way this Hadith(حديث) that I just mentioned, is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

675
00:45:42,762 --> 00:45:47,382
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًاكَثِيْرَا

